          <output>I executed the `A01_01_CreatePlan` task's instructions: resolved `authorativeSources` against the whitelisted Core packages, inspected `is`/`documentation`/`references` on the `org.blockml.bml.documentation.*` guides and the underlying `core`/`definition`/`type`/`constraint` Blocks they describe, and redesigned `org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a01_planning.data.BmlDocSetPlan` from scratch (treating the previous plan as non-authoritative, per the task's own instructions).

Key finding: the prior plan (from run T00005) omitted dedicated pages for roughly half of the 32 concepts mandated in `contents` (e.g. Blocks, Inheritance, Identifiers and References, Primitive/Struct/Enum Types, Primitive Entities, Types and Values, Members, Properties, Aggregations, Associations, Multiplicity and Collections, Suggestions, Embedded Blocks) — confirming it needed to be redesigned rather than reused.

New TOC (`RootPageGroup → DocsPageGroup`, 8 sub-groups, all ≤8 entries, within `maxGroupSize=30`):
- Getting Started (2), Foundations (7), Type System (7), Members (8), Behaviour &amp; Values (4), Composition &amp; Structure (4), BML: The Authoring Format (2), plus the `TableOfContents` index page.

Every one of the 32 required concepts now has its own `PagePlan` with scopes grounded in the corresponding authoritative source Block (e.g. `docs.Inheritance` grounded in `ModelingGuidelines`/`StructuralDefinition`'s abstract/final/baseType semantics; `docs.Suggestions` grounded in `ConstraintsModel`'s suggestions section).

`BmlDocSetPlan` was already exported in `Library.bml`, so no catalog change was needed. `npx blockml validate --all` shows no errors/warnings on the file (the pre-existing errors in the repo belong to unrelated future-sector task references, not this change).
</output>
          <completedAt>2026-09-13T20:35:24</completedAt>
          <task>
